  "washed": [],
  "read": "Fear held at 27 (28 this morning, 11 on Friday), but under the surface it was a rotation, not a rout. Good AI news kept getting sold: HPE (beat and raise) fell another −16%, Dell −12% into a report that then beat by a mile, and Nvidia lost Monday's 156.93 low on Huang's code-of-conduct admission. Bad news elsewhere was bought: equal-weight S&P +0.5%, health care +3.0%, staples +1.7%, small caps +0.5%. VIX fell from 28.9 to 26.4 while QQQ lost 2%: selling was concentrated, not panicked.",
  "positioned": "Hiding in defensives (XLV, XLP, XLRE) and out of chips (SMH −7.3%, −15% over a month). Hedges stay on (fear curve 1.03) with PCE and GDP at 8:30 tomorrow and a Dec 9 hike ~96% priced. Few are leaning long AI hardware into the holiday.",
  "surprise": "Dell's record backlog ($132.3B) and raised guide getting bought tomorrow, with SMH reclaiming today's 429.92 opening-range low and NVDA holding 150.50 (today's low), would catch the crowd that just left chips. The other side: a hot core PCE at 8:30 that pushes yields up would hit the defensives that got today's money as well."
